        // The constraints require state-changing calls on c be of the form c.f(...). For fallback we cannot use c.f; so we emulate by using c.sendMoney to transfer to c itself which will result in an external call to c and trigger its fallback.
        // Call sendMoney on c to make c call itself with value amountPaid, which will invoke fallback and increment depositsCount.
        bool sendMoneyReverted;
        try c.sendMoney(payable(address(c)), amountPaid) {
